planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
RE-MEASURED AT HEAD 192360e; I raised this slice from the audit register at the same HEAD.

THE WINDOW, EXACTLY. recovery-anchor-install.ts:224 runInstall ends with two publishes:
  fault?.("SWITCH");
  const switched = resealAnchorRecord(prepared, { currentSlot: prepared.targetSlot });
  await publishFileAtomically(anchorPath(request.anchorRoot), encodeAnchorRecord(switched));
  fault?.("INSTALLED_MARKER");
  const installed = resealAnchorRecord(switched, { state: "INSTALLED" });
  await publishFileAtomically(anchorPath(request.anchorRoot), encodeAnchorRecord(installed));
A crash between them leaves a durable record with currentSlot === targetSlot and state still "PREPARED".

THE MOST IMPORTANT FINDING: THE CODE ALREADY DESCRIBES THIS HAZARD AND THE GUARD IS ONE CONDITION SHORT. recovery-anchor.ts:100-106, the doc comment above settledInstall, reads: 'An install that already completed is NOT re-run. After the switch `currentSlot === targetSlot`, so re-entering the protocol would write the restored payload into the slot that is now LIVE - the one thing this module exists to never do.' But the guard itself (:108-115) is `if (stored.state !== "INSTALLED") return null;`. It covers only the fully-marked case. The post-switch/pre-marker record therefore falls through installRecoveryAnchor (:117-125) to prepareRecoveryAnchor + runInstall and re-enters the protocol - doing precisely what the comment forbids.

THE FIX NEEDS NO NEW DURABLE STATE. The record already carries everything required: currentSlot (recovery-anchor-contracts.ts:107), targetSlot (:121) and state (:120), and RECOVERY_ANCHOR_STATES is just PREPARED|INSTALLED. `currentSlot === targetSlot && state === "PREPARED"` is an unambiguous signature of a landed switch, because before the switch currentSlot names the OTHER slot.

WHAT RE-ENTRY ACTUALLY DOES, and why this is worth fixing despite being classified low: runInstall's first two steps are writeInactiveSlot and stampIncarnation, which reopen and WRITE the database in slotRoot. After the switch that slot is the live one, so re-entry writes the restored payload into the slot readers are currently resolving.

SIZES: recovery-anchor.ts 198 lines; recovery-anchor-install.ts 263 lines - ALREADY ABOVE the 250 target, which constrains where the marker-only helper can go. Tests: recovery-anchor.test.ts and recovery-anchor-refusals.test.ts.
